	"notes": "This is a type foundry's page showing off one typeface, and its trick is not columns, it's type that grows with the window. Six rows all say the word 'Timeline', each bigger than the last, and the letters are sized so a row nearly touches both edges of the screen whether you're on a phone or an ultrawide monitor — a small screen does not get smaller type, it just gets fewer of the huge rows before you have to scroll. Apart from the header, which drops from four items to three-plus-a-menu-button on a phone, the whole visible page is one plain column, top to bottom. The scan also shows a glyph-specimen grid and a footer much further down the page — this page is 17,000 to 35,000 pixels tall, and no single screenshot at a normal window height ever reaches that far, so the pictures alone would miss them entirely.",
